1
00:05:35,454 --> 00:05:41,454
A passion that cannot be denied. A betrayal that cannot be forgiven.

2
00:11:10,909 --> 00:11:16,909
Revenge is a thriller, romance, drama film directed by Tony Scott.

3
00:16:46,363 --> 00:16:52,363
Michael ‘Jay’ Cochran has just left the Navy after 12 years and he's not quite
sure what he's going to do, except that he knows he wants a holiday.

4
00:22:21,818 --> 00:22:27,818
He decides to visit Tiburon Mendez, a powerful but shady Mexican
businessman who he once flew to Alaska for a hunting trip.

5
00:27:57,272 --> 00:28:03,272
Arriving at the Mendez mansion in Mexico, he is immediately
surprised by the beauty and youth of Mendez’s wife, Miryea.

6
00:33:32,727 --> 00:33:38,727
Michael J. Cochran, played by Kevin Costner.

7
00:39:08,181 --> 00:39:14,181
Tiburon 'Tibey' Mendez, played by Anthony Quinn.

8
00:44:43,636 --> 00:44:49,636
Miryea, played by Madeleine Stowe.

9
00:50:19,090 --> 00:50:25,090
Amador, played by Miguel Ferrer.

10
00:55:54,545 --> 00:56:00,545
Cesar, played by Tomas Milian.

11
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
Mauro, played by Joaquín Martínez.

12
01:07:05,454 --> 01:07:11,454
Revenge is a 1990 American neo-noir romantic thriller film directed by Tony Scott and starring
Kevin Costner, Anthony Quinn, Madeleine Stowe, Miguel Ferrer and Sally Kirkland.

13
01:12:40,909 --> 01:12:46,909
Some scenes were filmed in Mexico.

14
01:18:16,363 --> 01:18:22,363
The film is a production of New World Pictures and Rastar
Films and was released by Columbia Pictures.

15
01:23:51,818 --> 01:23:57,818
Revenge also features one of John Leguizamo's earliest film roles.

16
01:29:27,272 --> 01:29:33,272
The film is based on a novella written by Jim Harrison,
published in Esquire magazine in 1979.

17
01:35:02,727 --> 01:35:08,727
Harrison co-wrote the script for the film.

18
01:40:38,181 --> 01:40:44,181
The film received a cult following since its release
especially for its dark theme and Scott's direction.

19
01:46:13,636 --> 01:46:19,636
It was remade in Pakistan twice as Zid (1991) and Baghi (2001).

20
01:51:49,090 --> 01:51:55,090
The film explores themes of mexico, revenge,
betrayal, revenge motive, revenge killing.

21
01:57:24,545 --> 01:57:30,545
The tone is emotional and intense.
